We shall need to define the \textit{Frobenius norm} and \textit{inner product} for this and later sections. Let $\mathcal{A} = \llbracket a_{ijk} \rrbracket_{i,j,k=1}^{l,m,n}$ and $\mathcal{B} = \llbracket b_{ijk} \rrbracket_{i,j,k=1}^{l,m,n}  \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n \times n}$. Then we define:
\[
\lVert \mathcal{A} \rVert_F^2 := \sum_{i,j,k=1}^{l,m,n} \lvert a_{ijk} \rvert^2, \qquad \langle \mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B} \rangle := \sum_{i,j,k=1}^{l,m,n} a_{ijk} b_{ijk}.

